#!/bin/bash
# Synthesis of the WebSky kappa map at nside 64 on one Datarmor node, with
# 1, 4, 16 and 28 MPI ranks, from the same initial map as the STL-Dev
# reference (fixtures/synthesis), so that the trajectories can be compared.
#
#   cd $W/runs && qsub -v W=$W $W/src/tools/datarmor/synth_nside64.pbs
#
# $W holds env.sh (tools/datarmor/env.sh), src/, target/ and data/.
#PBS -N stl-synth64
#PBS -q mpi_1
#PBS -l select=1:ncpus=28:mpiprocs=28:mem=60gb
#PBS -l walltime=01:00:00
#PBS -j oe
#PBS -m n
#PBS -S /bin/bash

set -u
W=${W:-/home1/scratch/jmdeloui/stl-mpi}
source "$W/env.sh"
OUT="$W/runs/${PBS_JOBID%%.*}"
mkdir -p "$OUT"
cd "$OUT"
FIX=$(ls -d "$W"/src/fixtures/synthesis/synthesis_kap_nside64*/ | head -1)
echo "job $PBS_JOBID on $(hostname), $(wc -l < "$PBS_NODEFILE") slots, fixture $FIX"
# Runs "ranks:block_pixels": rank scaling at the default block size, then
# the block-size dependence of the per-rank peak memory on one rank.
for RUN in ${RUNS:-1:16384 4:16384 16:16384 28:16384 1:4096 1:1024}; do
    P=${RUN%%:*}; B=${RUN##*:}; TAG=p${P}_b${B}
    echo "=== $P ranks, blocks of $B pixels"
    /usr/bin/time -v mpirun -np "$P" -machinefile "$PBS_NODEFILE" \
        "$CARGO_TARGET_DIR/release/stl-synth" \
        --target "$W/data/kap_nside64_nested.npy" \
        --init "$FIX/initial_map.npy" --init-units standardized --init-noise 0 \
        --block-pixels "$B" --niter 20 --out "$OUT/$TAG" 2> "$OUT/$TAG.time" | tee "$OUT/$TAG.log"
    grep -E 'Maximum resident|Elapsed' "$OUT/$TAG.time"
done
echo "done $(date)"
